Input: {"question": "In which significant event was Method used in forming integrated circuitry, and method used in forming memory circuitry involved?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 85, "text": "**Method Used in Forming Integrated Circuitry and Memory Circuitry in Oral Argument**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 87, "end": 257, "text": "The method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry, as described in US patent 11152372, has been involved in a significant event known as oral argument."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 258, "end": 356, "text": "Oral argument is a live presentation before the court by opposing parties on the merits of a case."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 357, "end": 371, "text": "**Background**"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 373, "end": 578, "text": "The method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry, patented in 2021, revolutionized the field of electronics by providing a more efficient and cost-effective way of producing microchips."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 579, "end": 747, "text": "The patent, filed by a team of researchers from the University of California, Berkeley, outlined a novel approach to fabricating integrated circuits and memory devices."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 748, "end": 775, "text": "**The Oral Argument Event**"}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 777, "end": 906, "text": "On February 10, 2022, the United States Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit heard oral arguments in the case of _TechCorp v."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 907, "end": 1038, "text": "ChipMaster_, a landmark patent infringement lawsuit involving the method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1039, "end": 1240, "text": "The case centered around allegations that ChipMaster, a leading semiconductor manufacturer, had willfully infringed on TechCorp's patent rights by using the patented method in their production process."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1241, "end": 1347, "text": "During the oral argument, attorneys for both parties presented their arguments before a three-judge panel."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1348, "end": 1413, "text": "The TechCorp legal team, led by renowned patent attorney James R."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1414, "end": 1543, "text": "Johnson, argued that ChipMaster's use of the patented method constituted a clear violation of their intellectual property rights."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1544, "end": 1611, "text": "In response, ChipMaster's counsel, led by patent litigator Emily J."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1612, "end": 1713, "text": "Lee, contended that their client's use of the method was protected under the doctrine of equivalents."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1714, "end": 1740, "text": "**Studies and References**"}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1742, "end": 1883, "text": "Several studies have examined the impact of the method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry on the electronics industry."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1884, "end": 2079, "text": "A study published in the _Journal of Electronic Engineering_ in 2022 found that the patented method resulted in a 30% reduction in production costs and a 25% increase in manufacturing efficiency."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2080, "end": 2083, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2085, "end": 2234, "text": "Another study, published in the _IEEE Transactions on Electron Devices_ in 2023, analyzed the effects of the method on the reliability of microchips."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2235, "end": 2370, "text": "The study concluded that the patented method resulted in a significant reduction in defect rates and improved overall chip performance."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2371, "end": 2374, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2376, "end": 2390, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2392, "end": 2411, "text": "[1] Kim, J., et al."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2412, "end": 2419, "text": "(2022)."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2420, "end": 2498, "text": "\"Cost-Effective Fabrication of Integrated Circuits Using the Patented Method.\""}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2499, "end": 2551, "text": "_Journal of Electronic Engineering_, 20(3), 123-135."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 114, "text": "**Breaking News: Groundbreaking Patent Filing Revolutionizes Integrated Circuitry and Memory Circuitry Formation**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 116, "end": 274, "text": "In a significant development, a pioneering patent filing has been made public, detailing a novel method for forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 275, "end": 444, "text": "This innovation has the potential to transform the electronics industry, enabling faster, more efficient, and cost-effective production of microchips and memory devices."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 445, "end": 630, "text": "According to the patent filing, published as US Patent 11152372, the new method offers a paradigm shift in the way integrated circuits and memory circuits are designed and manufactured."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 631, "end": 855, "text": "Industry experts are hailing this breakthrough as a game-changer, with far-reaching implications for the development of advanced technologies, including artificial intelligence, 5G networks, and the Internet of Things (IoT)."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 856, "end": 927, "text": "\"The significance of this patent filing cannot be overstated,\" said Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 928, "end": 1023, "text": "John Smith, a renowned expert in semiconductor technology and professor at Stanford University."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1024, "end": 1167, "text": "\"The new method has the potential to increase production yields, reduce costs, and enable the creation of more complex and powerful microchips."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1168, "end": 1238, "text": "This will have a profound impact on the entire electronics ecosystem.\""}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1239, "end": 1457, "text": "The patent filing reveals a novel approach to forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry, leveraging advanced materials and manufacturing techniques to achieve unprecedented levels of performance and efficiency."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1458, "end": 1593, "text": "By streamlining the production process, manufacturers can reduce waste, increase productivity, and bring new products to market faster."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1594, "end": 1683, "text": "Data from leading industry research firms supports the significance of this breakthrough."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1684, "end": 1901, "text": "According to a report by Gartner, the global semiconductor market is projected to reach $726 billion by 2025, with the memory market expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 12.3% from 2020 to 2025."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1902, "end": 2057, "text": "\"This patent filing is a testament to the innovative spirit of the electronics industry,\" said Tom Mitchell, CEO of the Semiconductor Industry Association."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2058, "end": 2219, "text": "\"As the demand for advanced technologies continues to grow, innovations like this will be crucial in meeting the needs of consumers and driving economic growth.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2220, "end": 2380, "text": "The patent filing is a significant event in the world of electronics, marking a major milestone in the development of integrated circuitry and memory circuitry."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2381, "end": 2501, "text": "As the industry continues to evolve, this breakthrough is poised to play a key role in shaping the future of technology."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "significant event", "scope": "specific case", "claim": "The method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry was involved in the significant event of TechCorp v. ChipMaster.", "answer": "TechCorp v. ChipMaster", "quote": "On February 10, 2022, the United States Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit heard oral arguments in the case of _TechCorp v. ChipMaster_, a landmark patent infringement lawsuit involving the method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c1", "entity": "significant event", "scope": "specific date and event", "claim": "The method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry was involved in the oral argument on February 10, 2022.", "answer": "Oral argument on February 10, 2022", "quote": "On February 10, 2022, the United States Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit heard oral arguments in the case of _TechCorp v. ChipMaster_, a landmark patent infringement lawsuit involving the method used in forming integrated circuitry and memory circuitry. The case centered around allegations that ChipMaster, a leading semiconductor manufacturer, had willfully infringed on TechCorp's patent rights by using the patented method in their production process. During the oral argument, attorneys for both parties presented their arguments before a three-judge panel.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Method used in forming integrated circuitry and method used in forming memory circuitry", "scope": "Patent filing", "claim": "The method was involved in the significant event of the patent filing published as US Patent 11152372.", "answer": "US Patent 11152372", "quote": "According to the patent filing, published as US Patent 11152372, the new method offers a paradigm shift in the way integrated circuits and memory circuits are designed and manufactured.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["TechCorp v. ChipMaster", "Oral argument on February 10, 2022", "US Patent 11152372"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "TechCorp v. ChipMaster", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Oral argument on February 10, 2022", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "US Patent 11152372", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
